1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:10,409
A magnet, a steel pin and a copper wire!

3
00:00:10,679 --> 00:00:12,949
The pin and the wire are both metal.

4
00:00:13,239 --> 00:00:14,919
Which one will the magnet pull?

5
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:16,374
One, the steel pin.

6
00:00:17,624 --> 00:00:19,164
Two, the copper wire.

7
00:00:20,424 --> 00:00:21,444
Three, both.

8
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:24,440
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:30,792
Today, a brand-new theme begins, and it starts with magnets!

10
00:00:31,299 --> 00:00:33,749
A little pigeon is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:33,999 --> 00:00:35,239
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:35,364 --> 00:00:37,064
Pigeons love our void deck.

13
00:00:37,124 --> 00:00:39,424
Look up high, on the ledges and the pipes!

14
00:00:39,475 --> 00:00:40,935
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:41,205 --> 00:00:43,055
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:45,155
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:45,736 --> 00:00:47,066
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:47,266 --> 00:00:48,756
What a magnet is.

19
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:50,428
What attract means.

20
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:52,290
Magnetic materials.

21
00:00:52,792 --> 00:00:53,732
Are you ready?

22
00:00:54,172 --> 00:00:54,942
Three!

23
00:00:55,322 --> 00:00:55,982
Two!

24
00:00:56,352 --> 00:00:57,002
One!

25
00:00:57,422 --> 00:00:58,142
Go!

26
00:00:59,531 --> 00:01:00,421
Round one!

27
00:01:00,721 --> 00:01:02,381
Which one will the magnet pull?

28
00:01:02,681 --> 00:01:03,981
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:07,456 --> 00:01:08,436
Locked in!

30
00:01:08,564 --> 00:01:09,294
One!

31
00:01:09,434 --> 00:01:13,084
In Grandma's sewing box, a magnet picks up the steel pins.

32
00:01:13,144 --> 00:01:14,424
I have seen it!

33
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:15,284
Two.

34
00:01:15,484 --> 00:01:18,644
The copper wire is thinner and lighter, so it should be easier

35
00:01:18,664 --> 00:01:19,504
to pull.

36
00:01:19,554 --> 00:01:20,554
Three, both!

37
00:01:20,574 --> 00:01:23,244
They are both metal, and my magnet pulls metal.

38
00:01:23,464 --> 00:01:24,314
Easy!

39
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:27,840
Basil, your magnet is smooth and painted, like a toy.

40
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:29,660
Is it made of plastic?

41
00:01:30,306 --> 00:01:31,436
Look closer.

42
00:01:32,046 --> 00:01:35,686
Long ago, people found a special kind of rock that pulls on

43
00:01:35,706 --> 00:01:36,376
iron.

44
00:01:36,396 --> 00:01:39,656
A natural magnet is also called a lodestone.

45
00:01:40,177 --> 00:01:43,157
A lodestone is a magnet that comes from the ground.

46
00:01:43,347 --> 00:01:44,767
Nobody made it!

47
00:01:44,787 --> 00:01:47,597
Now look inside Basil's magnet.

48
00:01:48,177 --> 00:01:52,397
Under the paint, it is made of metal, usually iron or steel.

49
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:57,020
And magnets come in lots of shapes: bar, U-shaped, button, rod, ring

50
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,090
and horseshoe!

51
00:02:00,791 --> 00:02:01,951
Say it with me!

52
00:02:02,657 --> 00:02:05,757
A magnet is an object that is usually made of iron or

53
00:02:05,777 --> 00:02:06,627
steel.

54
00:02:09,256 --> 00:02:10,446
Be a steel pin!

55
00:02:10,726 --> 00:02:11,716
Shrink down.

56
00:02:11,986 --> 00:02:12,926
Quietly.

57
00:02:15,209 --> 00:02:18,119
You are a steel pin, lying on the test table.

58
00:02:18,859 --> 00:02:22,479
Beside you, the copper wire looks like a big orange pipe.

59
00:02:22,992 --> 00:02:26,822
Here comes the magnet, like a giant red and blue tower.

60
00:02:27,592 --> 00:02:30,442
It is still far away, so nothing happens.

61
00:02:30,961 --> 00:02:32,541
Closer, and closer.

62
00:02:33,331 --> 00:02:34,541
You feel a tug.

63
00:02:35,331 --> 00:02:36,331
Then whoosh!

64
00:02:37,101 --> 00:02:40,411
You slide across the gap, and click onto the magnet.

65
00:02:40,932 --> 00:02:42,502
The magnet lifts you up.

66
00:02:43,312 --> 00:02:44,312
Look down.

67
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:48,402
The copper wire and the eraser have not moved at all.

68
00:02:50,061 --> 00:02:52,251
The answer is one: the steel pin!

69
00:02:52,511 --> 00:02:54,051
Did you show one finger?

70
00:02:54,321 --> 00:02:55,683
Put one finger up!

71
00:02:55,703 --> 00:02:58,263
The magnet pulled the steel pin across the gap.

72
00:02:58,333 --> 00:03:00,666
But the copper wire did not move at all!

73
00:03:00,686 --> 00:03:04,186
Pip, the copper wire is very light, but the magnet still did

74
00:03:04,206 --> 00:03:05,166
not pull it.

75
00:03:05,436 --> 00:03:07,636
So being light is not the reason.

76
00:03:07,774 --> 00:03:08,774
My turn!

77
00:03:08,904 --> 00:03:10,814
I tested Mum's iron wok.

78
00:03:10,864 --> 00:03:14,024
The magnet could not lift it, so the wok is not attracted

79
00:03:14,044 --> 00:03:15,114
to the magnet!

80
00:03:15,244 --> 00:03:16,804
Something is not right.

81
00:03:17,074 --> 00:03:19,254
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

82
00:03:19,534 --> 00:03:20,494
Hold on!

83
00:03:25,907 --> 00:03:27,037
Arms crossed?

84
00:03:27,307 --> 00:03:28,517
One finger up!

85
00:03:28,569 --> 00:03:29,439
Watch.

86
00:03:29,699 --> 00:03:32,449
When I let go, the magnet holds on to the side of

87
00:03:32,469 --> 00:03:33,089
the wok.

88
00:03:33,429 --> 00:03:35,039
The wok is attracted.

89
00:03:35,269 --> 00:03:37,269
It is just too heavy to lift!

90
00:03:37,396 --> 00:03:41,046
A fridge magnet cannot lift your fridge either, but it holds on

91
00:03:41,066 --> 00:03:42,196
to the fridge door.

92
00:03:42,319 --> 00:03:44,649
So my magnet sticks to the wok, like glue!

93
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:46,399
Is my magnet sticky?

94
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:49,170
Look closer, in slow motion.

95
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:53,060
The pin starts to move before it touches the magnet.

96
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:55,294
It jumps across the gap.

97
00:03:55,314 --> 00:03:57,534
The magnet pulls the pin towards it.

98
00:03:58,104 --> 00:04:00,654
We say the magnet attracts the pin.

99
00:04:01,444 --> 00:04:02,634
Attract means pull!

100
00:04:02,774 --> 00:04:05,554
My magnet pulls the pin, even before they touch.

101
00:04:05,684 --> 00:04:07,240
So it is not sticky at all!

102
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:10,100
The pin is made of steel, and the nail is made of

103
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:10,920
iron.

104
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,210
They are made of magnetic materials.

105
00:04:14,727 --> 00:04:18,497
Magnetic materials are the materials that a magnet attracts.

106
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:21,417
Iron and steel are magnetic materials!

107
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,420
Say it with me!

108
00:04:26,129 --> 00:04:29,429
Magnets attract objects made of magnetic materials.

109
00:04:29,929 --> 00:04:32,669
Magnetic materials include iron and steel.

110
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,609
Show me your score hand!

111
00:04:36,889 --> 00:04:38,279
One finger or more?

112
00:04:38,599 --> 00:04:39,959
You beat the Buddies.

113
00:04:40,229 --> 00:04:41,259
Two fingers?

114
00:04:41,539 --> 00:04:42,549
High five!

115
00:04:43,121 --> 00:04:44,571
Did you spot the pigeon?

116
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,981
It was on top of the bicycle rack!

117
00:04:47,110 --> 00:04:48,590
Here is a fun fact!

118
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:52,100
Scientists think pigeons can sense the Earth's magnetism.

119
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:55,750
It helps them find their way home, even from far away!

120
00:04:55,877 --> 00:04:57,157
Tell someone at home!

121
00:04:57,886 --> 00:05:00,086
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:05:00,376 --> 00:05:01,136
Ready?

123
00:05:01,423 --> 00:05:02,283
Magnet.

124
00:05:03,634 --> 00:05:04,434
Attract.

125
00:05:05,882 --> 00:05:07,382
Magnetic materials.

126
00:05:09,367 --> 00:05:10,307
Well done!

127
00:05:11,104 --> 00:05:11,804
Wait!

128
00:05:11,884 --> 00:05:14,374
Copper is a metal, just like iron and steel.

129
00:05:14,584 --> 00:05:17,218
So why does my magnet ignore the copper wire?

130
00:05:17,238 --> 00:05:18,828
Find out in Part Two!

131
00:05:19,988 --> 00:05:21,089
Say it with us!

132
00:05:21,889 --> 00:05:22,639
Ready?

133
00:05:22,763 --> 00:05:23,423
One!

134
00:05:23,763 --> 00:05:24,463
two!

135
00:05:24,768 --> 00:05:25,943
Now you know!
